---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/base-layout.astro";
import CaseStudyNav from "@organisms/case-study-nav/case-study-nav.astro";
import Hero from "@organisms/hero/hero.astro";
import FactsStrip from "@organisms/facts-strip/facts-strip.astro";
import Fact from "@molecules/fact/fact.astro";
import StatsStrip from "@organisms/stats-strip/stats-strip.astro";
import Stat from "@molecules/stat/stat.astro";
import TextSection from "@organisms/text-section/text-section.astro";
import CardGrid from "@organisms/card-grid/card-grid.astro";
import InfoCard from "@molecules/info-card/info-card.astro";
import StepList from "@organisms/step-list/step-list.astro";
import StepRow from "@molecules/step-row/step-row.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Modernizing a 10-year-old platform without stopping delivery · Nico Collin"
  description="How I modernize a legacy Java and AngularJS platform at Nurun, improving frontend architecture, build tooling, and CI while three squads keep shipping."
  noindex
  brand="spec"
>
  <Hero
    type="page"
    eyebrow="Case study 02 · Nurun · 2023–present"
    title="Modernizing a 10-year-old platform without stopping delivery"
    lead="As frontend tech lead on a multi-brand automotive account, I modernize a 10-year-old content-driven Java platform while three squads keep shipping. Instead of a rewrite, client work becomes the vehicle for improving the stack, one module and one block at a time."
  />

  <FactsStrip>
    <Fact label="Role" value="Frontend tech lead, supporting 3 squads (~15 people)" />
    <Fact label="Client" value="Large multi-brand automotive client, through Nurun" />
    <Fact label="Stack" value="Java with FreeMarker, AngularJS, Vue.js, Vite, Playwright" />
    <Fact label="Scope" value="Feature architecture, platform modernization, build and CI, testing, team coaching" />
  </FactsStrip>

  <StatsStrip>
    <Stat value="2×" caption="faster CI pipeline" />
    <Stat value="3" caption="squads kept shipping" />
    <Stat value="Vite" caption="replacing Gulp" />
  </StatsStrip>

  <TextSection id="context" index="01" title="Context">
    <p>The client platform is a content-driven Java application built on a dynamic block system, with more than 10 years of history. It renders on the server with FreeMarker, with legacy AngularJS on the frontend. Before I joined, Vue.js had been chosen to gradually replace AngularJS.</p>
    <p>As frontend tech lead, I define the technical approach for every new feature, support three squads of about 15 people, and am responsible for improving the project’s frontend stack.</p>
    <!-- TODO: what the platform is for (brand websites? a configurator?), its rough size,
         and the state it was in when you joined: what hurt most? -->
  </TextSection>

  <CardGrid
    id="challenges"
    index="02"
    title="Challenges"
    intro="The platform had to keep shipping for the client while it changed."
  >
    <InfoCard tag="01" title="No full rewrite"
      text="A complete AngularJS migration wasn’t an option, so modernization had to be incremental." />
    <InfoCard tag="02" title="Tangled CSS and JS"
      text="Styles and scripts were mixed together, so moving or cleaning anything risked regressions." />
    <InfoCard tag="03" title="Three squads, one platform"
      text="All three squads had to stay aligned, and knowledge had to spread across them instead of staying in one squad." />
    <!-- TODO: any other constraint, such as budget, client expectations or release cadence -->
  </CardGrid>

  <StepList
    id="approach"
    index="03"
    title="Approach"
    intro="Rather than a big-bang migration, I modernize the platform piece by piece, inside normal client work."
  >
    <StepRow number="01" title="Turn client requests into refactoring opportunities">
      <p>Any client request touching an AngularJS module becomes a chance to refactor it to Vue.js, when budget and time allow.</p>
      <!-- TODO: how much has been migrated so far, and how refactoring time is negotiated with the client -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="02" title="Load only what each block needs">
      <p>I evolved the block system from a single global CSS and JS file to loading only the files needed by the blocks on the page.</p>
      <!-- TODO: how it works technically, and its impact on page weight or performance scores -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="03" title="Introduce a BFF API">
      <p>I introduced a backend-for-frontend (BFF) API layer.</p>
      <!-- TODO: why it was needed and what problem it solved -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="04" title="Modernize the build and delivery pipeline">
      <p><strong>Gulp to Vite.</strong> I moved the build process from Gulp to Vite.</p>
      <p><strong>A CI pipeline twice as fast.</strong> I restructured the pipeline to run processes in parallel, cutting its run time in half.</p>
      <p><strong>Quality gates.</strong> CI/CD gates with linting and Stylelint enforce standards automatically.</p>
      <!-- TODO: build time before and after Vite -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="05" title="From Ghost Inspector to Playwright">
      <p>A major initiative moved end-to-end testing from Ghost Inspector to Playwright, bringing QA and developers into closer collaboration.</p>
      <!-- TODO: your role, why the switch, and what changed day to day for QA and developers -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="06" title="Spread knowledge across squads">
      <p><strong>Coaching.</strong> I coach the squad leads and the team.</p>
      <p><strong>Workshops.</strong> I facilitate workshops and collaboration across squads.</p>
      <p><strong>Documentation portal.</strong> A documentation portal exposes all architecture decisions and how to work on the platform.</p>
      <!-- TODO: who built the portal, and its format (for example, architecture decision records) -->
    </StepRow>
    <StepRow number="07" title="Bring AI into the workflow">
      <p>I explored AI tools and integrated them into the team’s workflow.</p>
      <!-- TODO: which tools, what for (code, docs, reviews, tests), how they were rolled out, what worked -->
    </StepRow>
  </StepList>

  <CaseStudyNav
    previous={{ href: "/case-studies/component-library", title: "Taking control of an inherited component library" }}
    next={{ href: "/case-studies/tecsys-design-practice", title: "Building a frontend and design practice from zero" }}
  />
</BaseLayout>